/-!
# Octad and heptad cocode calculations for H.15.2

The native octad kernel fixes precisely the six-dimensional supported pair
space. Its actual quotient acts as the natural split orthogonal Omega group;
the incident M23 stabilizer acts as A7 on the even seven-coordinate model.
The source orbit-avoidance bounds are three and four. Noncyclic kernel
subgroups have the same fixed space; nonidentity cyclic fixed spaces span
the parity hyperplane. The kernel induces every transvection with this axis,
and its identification with the additive axis respects stabilizer conjugation.

Native involution classification discharges all representative hypotheses:
Sylow-central M24 involutions and all M23 involutions have cocode codimension
four, and the other M24 class has codimension five. The pointwise centralizer
of the first class's fixed space is precisely its generated cyclic group.
The hexad application supplies the earlier M24 premises of the existing
marked M22 quotient and proves its fixed dimensions and full transvections.

These are H.14.4(3) for M24/M23 and H.15.2(2--6) for M24/M23. The separate
H.15.2(1) offender-uniqueness argument is not asserted here.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, combined manuscript of 1 March 2004,
printed pp.397--399.
-/
